      "created_at": "2018-04-16T16:44:04Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-04-16T16:46:03Z",
      "body": "a possible more-aggressive misuse of this for spearphishing, under the assumption that IS is being used as an authN/Z layer for something allowing private details to be added:\r\n\r\n1. malicious user (M) knows target user (T)'s name as provided by an external SSO identity provider (X).  I'll assume T has not yet used the system protected by IS, but has used X before\r\n2. M links an account they control in IS to T's account in X\r\n3. T logs in via X, thinking someone (their admin / service provider / automatic provisioning) had set up the account link for them\r\n4. T enters private information (SSN, HIPAA/GDPR-protected info, etc)\r\n5. M now has access to this information\r\n\r\nPreventing step 2 in this chain would be the purpose of this request - I would argue it to be a relatively serious security hole.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
      "reactions": {
